#AF87FF]schema[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]schema: add `link_reference` and `link_rendering` frontmatter to flat [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes, web descriptors, and strands, with strand-over-web-over-default [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]precedence, validation, and `closure:` accepted as a legacy alias.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Link scanner and target resolver[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]scan[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]scan: add the `[\\[target]]` / `![\\[target]]` body scanner that skips code [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]zones, plus a resolver that maps a raw target onto a flat note, web [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]descriptor, or strand.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Links in the closure walk[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]closure[dim] · [dim][/dim]after schema, scan[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]closure: classify each detected link as an inline or reference edge from[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the effective strategies, feed inline edges into the existing BFS [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through `precomputed_spans`, add cross-unit inline targets as extra [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]roots, and make ACE strand relations follow the same rules.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Linked References output[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]render[dim] · [dim][/dim]after closure[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]render: emit a numbered `## Linked References` section for every note [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and web unit across the markdown, rich, and json formats, and carry link[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]data in the JSON payloads.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Declare existing web strategies[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]migrate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after render[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrate: state `glossary`'s implicit/inline strategies explicitly, drop [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the legacy `closure:` key from in-repo descriptors, and report [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unresolved links as doctor and init warnings.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Generated task-type strand links[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]taskgen[dim] · [dim][/dim]after render[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]taskgen: make the generated task-type strands emit a Related Task Types [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section linking every other catalog type their own prose names.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Link the existing corpus[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]content[dim] · [dim][/dim]after migrate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]content: add links across the hand-authored notes and strands that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]already cross-reference each other in prose, and record the decision [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that supersedes the \"not a new, parallel link syntax\" clause of the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-webs record.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Skill and documentation updates[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after migrate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: teach `/sase_memory_write` to author links, and document the two [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]strategies in `docs/memory.md` and the generated memory README.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tr